00:03:22.355 --> 00:03:24.598
- I wanna fup fup fup
but I'm broken hearted

00:03:24.598 --> 00:03:26.039
(laughter)

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.622
- Oh that one, okay

00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:30.032
- I've heard two of these songs because

00:03:30.032 --> 00:03:32.141
I'm musically illiterate.
But, I'm gonna go with

00:03:32.141 --> 00:03:33.506
"Attention" by Charlie Puth

00:03:33.506 --> 00:03:34.838
- (Lana sings "Attention")

00:03:34.838 --> 00:03:36.246
- 'Cause that's the one
I bounce to the most.

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:37.807
- That bassline, it's so good.

00:03:37.807 --> 00:03:39.934
(mimics song)

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.101
That's not it.

00:03:41.608 --> 00:03:43.858
(laughter)

00:03:44.014 --> 00:03:45.931
Uh, I'm gonna go with "Solo"

00:03:45.931 --> 00:03:47.487
- "One Kiss" is the uh--

00:03:47.487 --> 00:03:48.717
- (Noah sings "One Kiss")

00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:50.900
- That one, yeah that's
the one. "One Kiss".

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.678
- See, I'm getting a bunch of songs

00:03:52.678 --> 00:03:54.845
I'm ridin solo, ridin solo

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:55.859
(laughter)

00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:56.700
That's what I'm singing

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.750
- By Jason Derulo?

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.000
- Jason Derulo!

00:03:59.268 --> 00:04:02.205
- Finally, choose a Korean
dish to gobble down.

00:04:02.205 --> 00:04:03.038
Kimchi,

00:04:03.283 --> 00:04:04.116
bibimbap,

00:04:04.592 --> 00:04:06.077
I don't know how to
pronounce that, I'm sorry.

00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:06.910
T-- Tteok?

00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:09.106
- Are you sweating?
- A little bit.

00:04:09.106 --> 00:04:09.939
- Are you nervous?

00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:12.000
- [Noah] Bulgogi, Bossam,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:12.917
or Japchae.

00:04:13.607 --> 00:04:14.779
I only know what kimchi is.

00:04:14.779 --> 00:04:16.879
- I'm gonna go with the bibimap.

00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:17.763
- That's a good one.

00:04:17.763 --> 00:04:19.096
- I pick kimchi.

00:04:21.563 --> 00:04:22.730
- I got Peter.

00:04:23.004 --> 00:04:24.131
- I got Chris.

00:04:24.131 --> 00:04:25.189
- Yes!
- Wait--

00:04:25.189 --> 00:04:26.285
I got Lara Jean.

00:04:26.285 --> 00:04:27.399
And I actually, truly,

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.796
I wasn't doing that on purpose.

00:04:29.796 --> 00:04:31.792
Kind, funny, and a little shy,

00:04:31.792 --> 00:04:34.141
you have a big heart
and a lot of feelings.

00:04:34.141 --> 00:04:35.800
Don't be afraid to wear
your heart on your sleeve

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.624
from time to time, and trust your instinct

00:04:37.624 --> 00:04:38.716
when it comes to love.

00:04:38.716 --> 00:04:40.222
- Confident, funny, and charming.

00:04:40.222 --> 00:04:42.885
You put on a hard exterior, when

00:04:42.885 --> 00:04:45.620
you're really a softie on the inside.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.438
You care deeply about
your friends and family

00:04:47.438 --> 00:04:50.339
and would go above and beyond
to be there if they needed you

00:04:50.339 --> 00:04:51.494
- You feel like you're confident?

00:04:51.494 --> 00:04:52.792
Do you feel like you're funny?

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:53.983
- Oh this is just a quiz.

00:04:53.983 --> 00:04:55.516
- Do you feel like you're charming?

00:04:55.516 --> 00:04:57.132
- I can be in the right instances,

00:04:57.132 --> 00:04:59.214
but most of the time,
I'm charmingly like--

00:04:59.214 --> 00:05:01.202
(crickets)

00:05:01.202 --> 00:05:02.921
- Outgoing, funny, and deeply loyal.

00:05:02.921 --> 00:05:04.968
You're someone who isn't afraid
to stand up for your beliefs

00:05:04.968 --> 00:05:07.166
While sometimes your mouth
can get you into trouble,

00:05:07.166 --> 00:05:07.999
- Yep.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.457
- True. You wouldn't trade
your extroverted ways

00:05:10.457 --> 00:05:11.386
for anything.

00:05:11.386 --> 00:05:13.292
- Do you think you're an extrovert?

00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:15.591
- I charge introvertedly, and then I like,

00:05:15.591 --> 00:05:16.424
(snaps)

00:05:16.424 --> 00:05:17.548
super out-going.

00:05:17.548 --> 00:05:19.946
- He really has a great
grasp on his personality.

00:05:19.946 --> 00:05:21.279
As you can tell.

00:05:22.174 --> 00:05:23.626
- We actually talked about this,

00:05:23.626 --> 00:05:24.710
like on set. We were like,

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.633
You could have played Peter, like

00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:27.849
I could have played Josh.

00:05:27.849 --> 00:05:29.916
Like it could have gone
either way we felt.

00:05:29.916 --> 00:05:31.249
- You are Peter.

00:05:31.341 --> 00:05:32.174
And I am--

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:33.389
I'm honored.

00:05:34.039 --> 00:05:35.148
- Can I be a part of this?

00:05:35.148 --> 00:05:37.172
- [Noah] I kinda wish that I was Josh.

00:05:37.172 --> 00:05:38.715
(laughter)

00:05:38.715 --> 00:05:41.298
(upbeat music)

